      "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
      "body": "Hooks are the preferred way for writing stateful React components, but there are a few things about them that still lag behind the class component API: profiling (since DevTools just shows \u201chooks changed\u201d rather than which ones changed).\r\n\r\nBuilding on top of the initial named hooks release _and_ the experimental `enableProfilerChangedHookIndices` feature flag, the Profiler should show the \u201cnames\u201d of hooks that changed between renders. (Because this would be expensive to eagerly calculate, we would need to add a post-processing phase to the profiler, like Chrome has, where we loaded and parsed names<sup>1</sup>.) \r\n\r\nNote that this issue will also resolve #16477.\r\n\r\n<sup>1</sup> We may only want to do this for components that are still mounted in the Fiber tree.",
